Suitcase_Climate.Transcription:
There's some new feathers on Bechan's head. I like helping her open the sheaths she can't reach;
it's so gratifying to see her new feathers blooming like a flower under the sun ...
Would you like to open one? You won't regret it.

Praise.Transcription:
It's amazing you can keep things so peaceful in here with so many people around.
I can't even stop a fight between my birdies. If they start pecking at each other, there's no use trying to separate them;
you've just got to hold out until there's a winner.

\u5165\u573a.Transcription:
I used to be afraid when I'd look through Glyndŵr's eyes;
soaring up so high can be truly frightening, but now I can dive from the highest cliff without hesitation ...
Because I know myself now. I wonder if you feel the same. Do you, Vertin?

To_the_Future.Transcription:
The lords and ladies told me the best future lies in the past ...
But I think they said that because they're scared. When I was bored in the blue room, I would reach my arm into an old mouse hole;
I wanted to explore, but when I got too scared, I'd pull my arm back out. That's kind of like what they're doing now.

Suitcase_Climate.Transcription:
The world of the living is very sensitive to change;
a short rain wets the ground, soaks your shirt, and snuffs out the light of my smudge stick.
Things in the land of the dead don't change much.

First_Encounter.Transcription:
You must be the Timekeeper! I've read about you in my notebooks;
they, I mean my past selves, would want to send their regards, but none of us have ever met you in person—
so, it's an honor to meet you!

Morning.Transcription:
Hey! Morning, Timekeeper! I was hanging out here before dawn,
waiting for a sunbath—it feels so good when I get that morning light on my leaves;
the warmth flows through my veins, driving my cold sap to run again ... I feel like I'm reborn.

Idle.Transcription:
„Ich lag einen ganzen Tag lang regungslos im Gebüsch;
nicht einmal, als der leblose Körper des Unteroffiziers auf mich fiel, wagte ich mich zu rühren.
Ich wartete und wartete, atmete so leise ich nur konnte, bis ihr Angriff endlich zum Stillstand kam.“

Intimacy.Transcription:
Andreas was lucky;
if he had not been found when he was, he would have lugged artillery until he dropped or been ridden into some foolish charge.
I ... hope that you might take him for a ride in the wilderness when you can. He would like that.

Morning.Transcription:
St. Petersburg was always foggy before sunrise;
that cold soggy air was a miserable commute for all the early birds ...
We're quite the lucky ones; at least we get to eat breakfast before going out on a mission.

Chitchat_II.Transcription:
I remember the day I joined the Foundation. "Congratulations. You're now an official member of the St. Pavlov Foundation."
Then they explained my duties, our regulations, and handed me a uniform;
it was so efficient it felt like an assembly line. I guess that's what makes it a great organization.

To_the_Future.Transcription:
Melusines value our privacy;
in fact, we can be downright monstrous about it.
So, for everyone else's sake, Laplace should really grant my request for a private lab, non?

Bond_Morning.Transcription:
We try to keep a consistent nightly routine;
you try sleeping with eight other voices awake and bickering in your head.
Still, we each have our own preferences. Sometimes a few of us like to sneak off at midnight to spend some time alone.

Night.Transcription:
Madam Lucy invited us to host a late-night show for Laplace Radio;
we're calling it "Fun Facts About Arcanum."
And with all nine of us behind the mic, it should be fun indeed! Care to make it ten?

Hobby.Transcription:
I love watching people. When they get surprised, scared, or excited;
I like figuring out what makes them smile or frown. Is it serotonin, cortisol, or adrenalin?!
Woof, I'm having a bit of a dopamine rush ...

Praise.Transcription:
In this industry, I've seen far too many friends turn into foes;
I've experienced it myself. But just as I began to think this was an inevitable fact of life, I met you.
Somehow, I see another possibility for how things could have ended.

It's amazing how you've managed to keep your friends safe in that suitcase;
it's like an island of your own!
I hope my future island can offer the same shelter for my friends.

Bond_Night.Transcription:
Mamãe Alda always said, "Neither love nor hate should weigh you down."
I wanted to tell her she was wrong! But her hugs were so warm at night;
she had the loveliest scent, like lilac; now whenever I smell it, I think of her.

To_the_Future.Transcription:
The wind always gives its signs.
The answer to the puzzle may have already been provided;
it's just that we have yet to discover it.

Hat_and_Hair.Transcription:
Only the head, or no head at all. And only once per night;
don't want the guests to get too accustomed to the horror,
and it'd get altogether tedious.

Chitchat_II.Transcription:
I have nothing against psychiatrists;
if only they would stop prying ... Always bragging about their mental strength,
forcing their help onto others, and perhaps worst of all, carrying that mirror with them ...
If they stop doing all that, I may just come to ... respect them.

To_the_Future.Transcription:
Best case scenario, people call me Professor or Doctor Windsong;
worse, they call me: liar, con woman;
do you know what is worse still? When they say nothing,
looking past me as if I was invisible.

First_Encounter.Transcription:
I'm Door, an insignificant piece of a mirror.
By nature I'm of no difference to my other 3587 siblings;
but knowing you has made me different to them.

Monologue.Transcription:
When in human society, do as the humans do;
when in the arcanist community, do as the arcanists do.
"Too attached to your identity" always causes arrogance and consequentially brings destruction.
